ass spectrometry, the latter of which is seeing growing adoption in the field. To address these gaps, we present Enveda-180, an open spectral library built from high-throughput, pooled characterization of 184,330 structurally diverse small molecules, more than doubling the combined structural coverage of MS/MS open libraries, and more than 5x the combined open CCS values. Compounds were profiled at three collision energies in both positive and negative ion modes. We describe our profiling methods in detail, including the use of ion mobility to resolve multiple species of the same nominal ion structure. Enveda-180 substantially expands the chemical space covered by open MS/MS libraries and enables multimodal learning by integrating retention time, CCS, MS/MS, and metadata within a single resource.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Krettler, Christoph A.", "affiliation": "Enveda", "orcid": "0000-0002-5709-3864"}, {"name": "Kind, Tobias", "affiliation": "Enveda", "orcid": "0000-0002-1908-4916"}, {"name": "DeBloois, Erik", "affiliation": "Enveda"}, {"name": "Killian, Marie", "affiliation": "Enveda"}, {"name": "Prince, John", "affiliation": "Enveda"}, {"name": "Taylor, James", "affiliation": "Enveda"}, {"name": "Gadiya, Yojana", "affiliation": "Enveda", "orcid": "0000-0002-7683-0452"}, {"name": "Domingo-Fern\u00e1ndez, Daniel", "affiliation": "Enveda", "orcid": "0000-0002-2046-6145"}, {"name": "Allen, August", "affiliation": "Enveda"}, {"name": "Colluru, Viswa", "affiliation": "Enveda"}, {"name": "Healey, David", "affiliation": "Enveda", "orcid": "0000-0002-9584-9757"}], "keywords": ["tandem mass spectrometry", "MS/MS", "ion mobility", "collision cross section", "CCS", "retention time", "spectral library", "metabolomics", "small molecules", "drug discovery", "Enamine"], "version": "v1.0.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/enveda/enveda-180", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}